<%- include("partials/head") %>
<%- include("partials/header") %>
<%- include("partials/nav") %>

<main class="resume-layout">
  <%- include("partials/contactModal") %>

  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="card project-detail-hero">
      <a href="/projects" class="project-back-link">Back to projects</a>
      <p class="project-tag">React PWA · TypeScript / Vite</p>
      <h1>unrealDice</h1>
      <p>
        A local-first dice management app for tabletop players who need
        reusable dice setups, safe backups and a tool that still works when the
        browser has no network connection.
      </p>

      <div class="project-detail-actions">
        <a
          href="https://unrealdice.onrender.com"
          class="project-link project-link-primary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Live Demo
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/STU6266/unreal-dice.git"
          class="project-link project-link-secondary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="project-detail-media-grid" aria-label="unrealDice visuals">
      <figure class="project-media-card">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/unrealdice/dashboard.png"
          alt="unrealDice dashboard with Quick Start, Create Group, My Groups, Import Backup, Coin and Random, and Install App options"
          width="1440"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Dashboard and tool navigation</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="project-media-card">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/unrealdice/quick-start.png"
          alt="unrealDice Quick Start page showing built-in dice templates with play and copy actions"
          width="1440"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Built-in dice set templates</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="project-media-card project-media-card--portrait">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/unrealdice/mobile-install.png"
          alt="Mobile unrealDice install screen with offline app installation instructions"
          width="390"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Mobile install and offline/PWA view</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-grid">
      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          unrealDice is not only a dice roller. It is a small product around a
          repeated user workflow: create dice groups once, reuse them during a
          game session, keep roll history available and export backups so local
          browser data is not the only copy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>React, TypeScript, Vite, React Router</li>
          <li>PWA setup with service worker and manifest</li>
          <li>localStorage-based persistence and JSON backups</li>
          <li>Vitest, Supabase for optional remote Quick Start templates</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Features</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Reusable dice groups with configurable sets, colors and modifiers</li>
          <li>Play mode with roll all, combo rolls and temporary dice locks</li>
          <li>Separate histories for rolls, coin flips and random tools</li>
          <li>Validated JSON import/export so backups do not overwrite data</li>
          <li>Installable PWA foundation with offline application shell</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          The app separates route screens, reusable components, domain helpers,
          focused hooks and storage services. Saved group definitions are kept
          apart from temporary play-state such as locked dice and active
          modifiers, which prevents a game session from accidentally changing a
          reusable setup.
        </p>
        <ol class="engineering-flow" aria-label="unrealDice engineering flow">
          <li>React UI</li>
          <li>App and session state</li>
          <li>Local-first storage</li>
          <li>Import/export backups</li>
          <li>PWA/offline use</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Challenges</h2>
        <p>
          The main challenge was making local-first behavior feel safe. Browser
          storage can be cleared, so backups matter. Importing a backup also
          needs guardrails: invalid files should fail clearly, and valid imports
          should create new IDs instead of overwriting existing groups.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>What I Learned</h2>
        <p>
          I practiced TypeScript state modeling, product thinking around repeat
          use, PWA/offline behavior, validation around user-owned data and the
          difference between persistent configuration and temporary session
          state.
        </p>
      </section>
    </section>
  </article>
</main>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
